      "title": "Adding A \"Not Found\" Route",
      "lectureOrder": 282,
      "videoOrder": 269,
      "sourceHash": "7dda9c26f8396c1e1b2d78872ca6c67ed6b9e639540f9bf184880f151b32d273",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.72,
          "end": 2.79,
          "en": "So what else can we do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.79,
          "end": 5.73,
          "en": "with the Angular router in this application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.73,
          "end": 9.273,
          "en": "and what else should you know about the Angular router?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.32,
          "end": 13.65,
          "en": "Well, for example, how we can handle the scenario",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.65,
          "end": 17.073,
          "en": "that a user tries to visit a page that doesn't exist.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.03,
          "end": 21.39,
          "en": "At the moment, this will lead to us going back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.39,
          "end": 23.37,
          "en": "to that starting page here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.37,
          "end": 26.373,
          "en": "but that might not be the behavior we want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.6,
          "end": 29.85,
          "en": "Instead, Angular allows you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.85,
          "end": 33.69,
          "en": "to define a so-called catch all route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.69,
          "end": 36.24,
          "en": "here as a last route typically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.24,
          "end": 39.453,
          "en": "where you set the path to two asterisk.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.56,
          "end": 42.75,
          "en": "And this route will then be activated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.75,
          "end": 44.97,
          "en": "if no other route is met.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.97,
          "end": 48.06,
          "en": "So if no other path matches the path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.06,
          "end": 50.283,
          "en": "that's currently entered in the URL.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.51,
          "end": 55.23,
          "en": "And you can then specify your fallback component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 55.23,
          "end": 57.63,
          "en": "And for this application here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.63,
          "end": 61.74,
          "en": "I actually prepared a component I want to use for that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 61.74,
          "end": 66.74,
          "en": "a component you find attached, the NotFoundComponent,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66.78,
          "end": 70.083,
          "en": "which I'll insert into my app folder next to the header.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 71.4,
          "end": 75.18299999999999,
          "en": "This is a component that simply outputs some fallback text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 76.17,
          "end": 78.513,
          "en": "And with that component added,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 81.21000000000001,
          "end": 84.06,
          "en": "we can use it here as a component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 84.06,
          "end": 87.18299999999999,
          "en": "for this fallback catch all route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 88.92,
          "end": 93.33,
          "en": "And that ensures that if I enter some invalid path,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 93.33,
          "end": 95.97999999999999,
          "en": "I see that fallback content here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 96.93,
          "end": 99.813,
          "en": "and the URL stays what it was before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 100.92,
          "end": 104.343,
          "en": "So that's another important feature to know about.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
